Duties & Responsibilities

Plans and manages inventory requirements for imported and long-lead-time spare parts, ensuring orders are placed sufficiently in advance to accommodate supplier and shipping lead times;
Prepares and maintains weekly buying reports to identify production shortages, SKU replenishment requirements and sales-related shortages;
Conducts daily inventory checks to maintain accurate stock levels and support uninterrupted production and operational requirements;
Analyses inventory movement trends and periodically update product group classifications to optimise stock levels and minimise excess, obsolete and slow-moving inventory;
Reviews and updates SKU stocking levels in collaboration with Branch Managers and relevant Heads of Department to ensure inventory is aligned with operational requirements;
Prepares and processes forward-order buying reports to support supplier planning and ensure future inventory requirements are communicated in advance;
Ensures all procurement and buying reports are accurate, complete and subject to the required checks and approvals before submission to the Procurement team;
Monitors inventory requirements and proactively identify potential supply shortages, stock risks and replenishment requirements;
Supports stock-taking activities by preparing inventory reports, reconciling results and investigating discrepancies;
Travels to assembly, fabrication and other operational locations when required to support inventory and procurement activities;

Desired Experience & Qualification

Matric/Grade 12;
Diploma or Degree in Supply Chain, Logistics, Inventory Management or a related field;
1–3 years’ experience
in inventory control, reporting or supply chain analytics;
Experience in
inventory replenishment and inventory data management;
Ability to analyse inventory data, identify trends and solve problems effectively.

